{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you shall guard yourself from every evil thing.</b> This warning is because of the holiness of the Ark, and so we find in the war against Midyan that the Ark went with them." "<b>And by way of</b> the plain sense (peshat): 'from every evil thing' — from everything evil that the Torah has forbidden, because the camps of the Canaanites when they went out to war would be set loose to do every abomination and every obscenity, and they conducted themselves with abandon in all things. Therefore Scripture warns the camp of Israel that they should guard themselves from all the evil things that the rest of the Canaanites practice and pay no heed to in time of war. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted (draw the midrash): 'from every evil thing' — these are forbidden sexual relations and evil speech. Forbidden sexual relations, from what is written: ״ולא יראה בך ערות דבר״ (Deuteronomy 23:15), and this is what it says: 'from every evil thing.' Evil speech, for it says 'from every evil thing,' that is, evil speech, and this is evil speech (לשון הרע). And Scripture wished to warn concerning these two because they are severe transgressions and the Shekhinah departs on their account. And further, our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in tractate Avodah Zarah: 'and you shall guard yourself from every evil thing' — lest a person entertain lustful thoughts by day and come to impurity by night. And this is what is juxtaposed to it: 'if there be among you a man who is not pure by reason of a nocturnal emission' (Deuteronomy 23:11). From here Rabbi Pinchas ben Yair said: watchfulness leads to alacrity, alacrity leads to cleanliness, cleanliness leads to abstinence, abstinence leads to purity, purity leads to holiness, holiness leads to fear of sin, fear of sin leads to humility, humility leads to piety, piety leads to the Holy Spirit. <b>The sage</b> of blessed memory mentioned here ten traits, five physical and five intellectual, and all of them lead to the tenth, which is the Holy Spirit."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:36.805298684Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}